k01 -- ANGLE 5: the acceleration census.  Which system classes have g_int crossing a_0, and what
      external field are they sitting in?  a_0 canonical 9.36e-11 / alt 1.13e-10 m/s^2.
======================================================================================================================

Sanity: a_0 = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_DE).  Sigma_M = a_0/(2 pi G) = 106.9 (canonical) / 129.0 (alt) Msun/pc^2
        the Sun's MOND radius r_M = sqrt(GM_sun/a_0) = 7961 / 7245 AU

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A.  SOLAR-SYSTEM-SCALE SYSTEMS  (external field = the Milky Way at R_sun)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Milky Way field at the Sun: g_ext = 2.166e-10 m/s^2 = 2.314 a_0 (canonical) / 1.917 a_0 (alt)
  => Newtonian-equivalent e = 1.6815 (canonical) / 1.3055 (alt);   nu(e) = 1.3763, L(e) = -0.2440
  => the EFE-saturation boost M_dyn/M_bar = nu(e)[1+L/3] = 1.2644 (canonical) / 1.3374 (alt)
  cross-check: the frozen Gaia DR4 wide-binary band gamma_v = 1.1614-1.1814 canonical means a FORCE boost gamma_v^2 = 1.3488-1.3957; alt 1.1917-1.2267 -> 1.4201-1.5048
  RECONCILIATION: the frozen registration adopts x_ext = 1.89929 a_0 (= 1.778e-10 m/s^2,
    i.e. V_c = 211 km/s at R_0 = 8.122 kpc).  With it,
    e = 1.28903, nu(e) = 1.47342 (registration quotes nu(y_extN) = 1.47342 -- matches),
    B = nu(e)[1+L/3] = 1.3414 canonical / 1.4314 alt.
  [PASS] the e-inversion reproduces the registration's own nu(y_extN) = 1.47342 at x_ext = 1.89929  [CAN FAIL]   (nu(e) = 1.473422)
    AGAINST INTEREST: B (the g_int -> 0 asymptote) sits -2.25% from the midpoint of the frozen
    wide-binary band gamma_v^2 = 1.3488-1.3957.  It is inside the band's lower edge but not at its centre,
    because the registered band comes from a full nonlinear TWO-BODY AQUAL solve at finite internal field,
    not from the point-mass asymptote.  2.2% is therefore the irreducible mismatch between
    the two rungs' own definitions, and it is a floor on how well this law can ever be tested.
    => NORMALISATION SYSTEMATIC on the law: B(R_sun) = 1.341 (registered field) to 1.264 (V_c = 233 km/s), canonical; 1.431 to 1.337, alt.
