THE CANDIDATE LAW THAT THE CENSUS POINTS AT
======================================================================================================================
  M_dyn/M_bar = nu(e)[1 + L(e)/3],   nu(e) e = g_ext/a_0,   g_ext = V_c^2/R,   a_0 = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_DE)
  for every self-gravitating system with g_int << g_ext inside a galaxy.  ONE number per Galactocentric
  radius, the same for a wide binary and a molecular cloud -- 15 decades of mass, no free parameter.

