======================================================================================================================
THE LAW RUN BACKWARDS -- the Milky Way's baryonic mass from a stellar velocity ratio alone
======================================================================================================================
  B is monotone in e, so a MEASURED boost inverts:  e = B^-1(B_hat),  M_b,MW = e a_0 R_0^2 / G.
  With B_hat = gamma_v^2 from Gaia DR4 wide binaries this measures the Galactic baryonic mass with
  NO photometry, NO stellar M/L and NO rotation curve -- only a velocity ratio and Lambda.

    gamma_v  B = gamma_v^2        e   M_b,MW canonical     M_b,MW alt
     1.1000         1.2100   2.0997          9.299e+10      1.123e+11
     1.1614         1.3488   1.2593          5.577e+10      6.733e+10
     1.1814         1.3957   1.0953          4.851e+10      5.856e+10
     1.1917         1.4201   1.0230          4.531e+10      5.470e+10
     1.2000         1.4400   0.9698          4.295e+10      5.186e+10
     1.2267         1.5048   0.8239          3.649e+10      4.405e+10
     1.2500         1.5625   0.7213          3.195e+10      3.857e+10

  SENSITIVITY: d log M_b / d log B = -4.21, i.e. d log M_b / d log gamma_v = -8.4.
  A 2% measurement of gamma_v therefore gives M_b,MW to 17%.
  The published Galactic baryon census is 6.2-6.7e10 Msun.  If December returns gamma_v in the frozen
  band, the canonical footing infers 4.9-5.6e10 (10-25% LOW) and the alt footing 5.9-6.7e10 (on the
  census).  That is a FOOTING DISCRIMINATOR that costs nothing extra -- but it is only non-circular
  once gamma_v is MEASURED, because the frozen band was itself computed from an assumed local field.
  [PASS] the backward inversion is well-posed: B is strictly monotone decreasing in e  [CAN FAIL]   (B(0.3) = 2.074 > B(1) = 1.429 > B(3) = 1.140 > B(10) = 1.020)

  UPSILON LEVER of the census itself: zero.  Every acceleration above is computed from a catalogued
  mass and radius, and the two classes the census promotes (globular clusters via M/L_V,dyn, molecular
  clouds via alpha_vir) carry dynamical masses, not photometric ones.  The stellar M/L enters only the
  GC rung's ABSOLUTE normalisation (lever -1), never the shape tests, and not at all for the clouds.

